        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e924b78c62384194891bc4ba41b067cd",
      "statement": "Peering uses one tunneled h1-upgraded duplex stream per peer (`/peer/tunnel`, protocol `celld-tunnel`, version 5, header `x-cells-tunnel-version`); inner traffic is literal HTTP; per-call control rides reserved `x-cells-*` headers that a node B strips for each case; idle tunnels are pooled with h1 keep-alive to avoid ephemeral-port exhaustion within seconds at loopback speed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/main/peer_tunnel.rs#L1-L20",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2bf3108470698d9cc7484d37ed9debd98e8cf237d09e7533851b7e0b0d34b82d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/main/peer_tunnel.rs#L34-L38",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:906fc304f23d22eff19d06a7e1b19a0522e390dddf0e10e7b3d0c7a0fcd3718a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8ce14e4a466747e9b37a99d600b73c46",
      "statement": "The peer protocol declares `PROTOCOL_VERSION = 5` (`x-cells-peer-version`) and the tunnel-establishment handshake carries that version so a later protocol change can negotiate instead of refuse; a mixed v0.3.x/v0.4.x fleet cannot proxy cell calls (fetch/RC/WebSocket) because the plain-HTTP-on-only tunnel is versioned.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/peer_auth.rs#L16-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1d2750773d5ea9b250e996d525ef0f90c4556103a913358325a3dcd07e408875:"
        },
